# LF everywhere, in the repository and on checkout. verify/run.sh is a bash
# script, and a CRLF checkout makes bash fail on it with a syntax error naming
# a token that ends in a carriage return (HonestFramework learned this once).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
# A round's ledger is archived byte for byte, as its authors wrote it: git
# stores those files as they are, carriage returns included.
docs/round2-ledger/** -text
